# The shortcut's store: readings come back as Readings, but outages come back as the lines they are kept as, and a
# summary is kept and given back as a line; the Outage that `save_outage` puts no get gives back, and no Summary type
# exists. `summary` returns the kept line when there is one (`return` in the `if let`), else reads the day's readings and
# writes the new line: the code after the early return is the other arm of that choice. A library's operation whose
# result the body names (`read_to_string`, `split`, `find`, `collect`, `fold`, the `next()`s a tuple binds), or that
# changes the String it runs on (`push_str`), is a step; what it touches stays its caller's. Each file is read, used and
# written by the route: it stands on both sides.
#
# #new: new-A a parameter at the own arrow by its type, new-B an own arrow taking every class its steps build, new-F a
# class's read-and-written place between, new-G an own arrow dropping a value it uses and hands on, new-L the code after
# an early return no arm, new-N `push_str` on a read String no step, new-O results a pattern binds no steps (see the
# report of #52's pair plans).

